---

## Requirements Analysis

### Core Objectives
1. **SQL Injection Prevention** — Sanitize dynamic query filters before they reach the database layer
2. **XSS Prevention** — Sanitize user profile input before storage and rendering

### Threat Model

| Threat | Vector | Mitigation |
|--------|--------|------------|
| SQL Injection (Classic) | `' OR '1'='1` | Parameterized query builder + whitelist validation |
| SQL Injection (Union) | `UNION SELECT * FROM users` | Keyword blacklist + structural validation |
| SQL Injection (Blind) | `1; WAITFOR DELAY` | Token type enforcement |
| XSS (Reflected) | `<script>alert(1)</script>` | HTML entity encoding + tag stripping |
| XSS (Stored) | Persistent script in profile | DOMPurify-style allowlist sanitizer |
| XSS (DOM-based) | `javascript:void(0)` | URL scheme validation |
| Second-order injection | Encoded payloads `%27` | Multi-pass decode + normalize |
| Unicode bypass | `＜script＞` | Unicode normalization (NFC) |

### Architecture

```
src/
├── validation/
│   ├── types.ts                    # Shared type definitions
│   ├── validators/
│   │   ├── base.validator.ts       # Abstract validator base
│   │   ├── sql.validator.ts        # SQL injection validator
│   │   └── xss.validator.ts        # XSS validator
│   ├── sanitizers/
│   │   ├── sql.sanitizer.ts        # SQL input sanitizer
│   │   └── xss.sanitizer.ts        # XSS/HTML sanitizer
│   ├── pipeline/
│   │   ├── pipeline.ts             # Composable validation pipeline
│   │   └── stages.ts               # Pre-built pipeline stages
│   ├── query/
│   │   ├── filter.builder.ts       # Safe parameterized query builder
│   │   └── filter.types.ts         # Filter type definitions
│   └── index.ts                    # Public API barrel
tests/
├── sql.validator.test.ts
├── xss.validator.test.ts
├── sql.sanitizer.test.ts
├── xss.sanitizer.test.ts
├── pipeline.test.ts
└── filter.builder.test.ts
```

### Design Decisions
- **Zero external sanitization libraries** — All logic is self-contained for auditability
- **Parameterized queries only** — Never string-interpolate user input into SQL
- **Allow-list approach** — Only permit known-safe patterns, deny everything else
- **Immutable pipeline** — Each stage returns a new value, no mutation
- **Typed result objects** — All functions return `ValidationResult<T>` discriminated unions

