### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

## System Overview

A production-grade organization member invitation system with:
- **Cryptographically secure tokens** (HMAC-SHA256 + random salt, 32-byte entropy)
- **Expiring invitations** (configurable TTL, default 72h)
- **Email dispatch** (async, templated, retry-safe)
- **Role assignment** (RBAC: owner, admin, member, viewer)
- **Full audit trail** (invitation lifecycle events)

## Architecture

```
src/
├── config/           # Environment + app configuration
├── db/               # Database layer (SQLite via better-sqlite3 for portability)
│   ├── schema.sql
│   ├── migrations/
│   └── client.ts
├── models/           # Domain models + repositories
│   ├── organization.ts
│   ├── invitation.ts
│   └── user.ts
├── services/         # Business logic
│   ├── invitation.service.ts
│   ├── email.service.ts
│   └── token.service.ts
├── routes/           # HTTP handlers (Express)
│   └── invitation.routes.ts
├── middleware/        # Auth, validation, error handling
│   ├── auth.ts
│   ├── validate.ts
│   └── error.ts
├── templates/        # Email HTML templates
│   └── invitation.html
├── types/            # Shared TypeScript types
│   └── index.ts
└── app.ts            # Express application bootstrap
tests/
├── unit/
│   ├── token.service.test.ts
│   ├── invitation.service.test.ts
│   └── email.service.test.ts
└── integration/
    └── invitation.routes.test.ts
```

## Security Considerations

- **Token generation**: `crypto.randomBytes(32)` + HMAC-SHA256 over `{tokenId}:{invitationId}:{expiry}` using server secret
- **Token storage**: Store only the HMAC signature hash in DB (never the raw token value)
- **Replay prevention**: Single-use tokens invalidated immediately on acceptance
- **Expiry enforcement**: DB-level TTL + service-level check
- **Rate limiting**: Per-organization invite rate limit (10/hour)
- **Email enumeration prevention**: Uniform response regardless of existing membership
- **Role escalation prevention**: Inviter cannot grant roles above their own

## Edge Cases

1. Re-invitation of existing member → idempotent (resend if pending, error if active)
2. Expired token acceptance → graceful error with re-invite prompt
3. Already-accepted token replay → 409 Conflict
4. Inviter loses permission mid-flow → token validation checks current inviter role
5. Organization deletion → cascade invalidates all pending invitations
6. Email delivery failure → async retry queue with exponential backoff
7. User self-invitation → prevented at service layer

