## Requirements Analysis

**Core Features:**
- Multi-file diff viewer with file tree navigation
- Monaco Editor diff view (side-by-side and inline modes)
- Git diff parsing from unified diff format
- Inline code review comments (add, edit, delete, resolve)
- Syntax highlighting per file language
- Keyboard shortcuts and accessibility

**Architecture Decisions:**
- **State Management:** Zustand for global state (lightweight, no boilerplate)
- **Diff Parsing:** Custom parser for unified diff format (`@@ -l,s +l,s @@` hunks)
- **Monaco Integration:** `@monaco-editor/react` wrapper with `DiffEditor` component
- **Comment Persistence:** In-memory with localStorage backup
- **Component Architecture:** Container/Presenter pattern with strict TypeScript

**Edge Cases:**
- Empty files (added/deleted entirely)
- Binary file diffs (skip rendering)
- Files with no newline at EOF
- Very large files (>10,000 lines) — virtual scrolling via Monaco
- Conflicting comment anchors when diff changes
- Unicode content in diffs
- Renames/mode changes in diff headers

**Security Considerations:**
- Sanitize comment content (no XSS — display via React text nodes, not dangerouslySetInnerHTML)
- Validate diff format before parsing
- No eval/dynamic code execution
- CSP-compatible (no inline scripts injected)

**File Structure:**
```
src/
  types/           # TypeScript interfaces
  store/           # Zustand state slices
  utils/           # Diff parser, language detector
