### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

---

#### 1.1 Requirements Analysis

**Functional Requirements:**
- Real-time terminal output rendering via WebSocket using xterm.js
- Auto-scrolling to bottom when new data arrives (with user-override: scroll-lock disables auto-scroll)
- Search/filter buffer: highlight or filter terminal output by regex or string
- WebSocket reconnection with exponential backoff + jitter
- Multiple terminal sessions (tab-based)
- Copy-to-clipboard of selected terminal text
- Terminal resize handling (fit addon)

**Non-Functional Requirements:**
- TypeScript strict mode throughout
- React 18 with hooks (no class components)
- Zero `any` types
- Production-grade error boundaries
- Memory-safe buffer management (ring buffer, max 10,000 lines)
- Accessible ARIA labels
- Complete unit & integration test stubs

---

#### 1.2 Architectural Decomposition

```
src/
├── types/
│   ├── terminal.ts          # All domain types
│   └── websocket.ts         # WebSocket state types
├── hooks/
│   ├── useWebSocket.ts      # WS connection + reconnection logic
│   ├── useTerminal.ts       # xterm.js lifecycle management
│   ├── useAutoScroll.ts     # Scroll-lock state machine
│   └── useSearch.ts         # Search buffer + highlighting
├── lib/
│   ├── RingBuffer.ts        # Fixed-size ring buffer
│   ├── WebSocketManager.ts  # Reconnection engine
│   └── SearchEngine.ts      # Regex/string search over buffer
├── components/
