### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

## Requirements Analysis

### Functional Requirements
- **Real-time terminal output**: Stream terminal data via WebSocket to an xterm.js instance
- **Auto-scrolling**: Automatically scroll to bottom on new data, pause when user scrolls up
- **Search buffer filtering**: Search through terminal buffer content with match highlighting
- **WebSocket reconnection**: Exponential backoff reconnection with configurable retry limits

### Non-Functional Requirements
- Type-safe TypeScript throughout (strict mode)
- React functional components with hooks
- Production-grade error handling
- Accessible UI components
- Memory-efficient buffer management

### Architecture

```
src/
├── types/
│   └── terminal.ts          # Shared TypeScript types/interfaces
├── hooks/
│   ├── useWebSocket.ts      # WebSocket connection + reconnection logic
│   ├── useTerminal.ts       # xterm.js lifecycle management
│   ├── useAutoScroll.ts     # Auto-scroll detection + control
│   └── useTerminalSearch.ts # Search buffer + match navigation
├── components/
│   ├── TerminalViewer.tsx   # Root orchestration component
│   ├── TerminalPane.tsx     # xterm.js mount + resize container
│   ├── SearchBar.tsx        # Search input + navigation controls
│   ├── StatusBar.tsx        # Connection status + scroll indicator
│   └── ConnectionOverlay.tsx # Reconnecting/disconnected overlay
├── utils/
│   ├── reconnection.ts      # Exponential backoff calculator
│   ├── bufferSearch.ts      # Buffer text search algorithm
│   └── ansiSanitizer.ts    # Strip/validate ANSI escape codes
├── constants/
│   └── terminal.ts          # Default config constants
└── index.tsx                # App entry point
```

### Edge Cases & Security

1. **XSS via terminal data**: All data written to xterm.js is treated as raw terminal bytes — xterm.js renders safely
2. **Memory leak**: Buffer capped at MAX_BUFFER_LINES; oldest lines evicted
3. **WebSocket URL injection**: URL validated against allowlist pattern
4. **Rapid reconnect storm**: Exponential backoff with jitter + max delay cap
5. **Search on large buffers**: Debounced search with Web Worker offloading pattern (synchronous fallback)
6. **ResizeObserver**: Properly cleaned up on unmount
7. **Multiple xterm instances**: Terminal disposed on component unmount
8. **Stale closures in WebSocket handlers**: Refs used for callbacks

