### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

---

## Requirements Analysis

**Core Features:**
- Multi-file diff viewer with file navigation/tree
- Monaco Editor powered side-by-side diff view
- Syntax highlighting per language detection
- Inline code review comments (threaded)
- Git diff parsing (unified diff format)
- Comment CRUD (add, edit, delete, resolve)

**Edge Cases:**
- Binary files (detect & skip rendering)
- Empty files, new files, deleted files
- Large diffs (virtualization hints)
- Conflict markers in diffs
- Unidiff with no newline at end
- Comment anchor drift when diff changes
- Monaco not loaded (lazy load guard)
- SSR environments (dynamic import guards)

**Security Considerations:**
- Sanitize comment content (no raw innerHTML)
- XSS prevention on file paths
- Input validation on comment submission
- No eval/dangerous APIs

**Architecture:**

```
src/
├── types/                     # TypeScript interfaces
│   ├── diff.ts                # DiffFile, DiffHunk, DiffLine
│   └── comment.ts             # ReviewComment, CommentThread
├── lib/
│   ├── diffParser.ts          # Parse unified diff → DiffFile[]
│   ├── languageDetect.ts      # File ext → Monaco language id
│   └── commentStore.ts        # Zustand store for comments
├── components/
│   ├── DiffViewer/
│   │   ├── DiffViewer.tsx      # Root orchestrator
│   │   ├── DiffViewer.css
│   │   ├── FileTree.tsx        # Left sidebar file navigation
│   │   ├── FileTreeItem.tsx
│   │   ├── MonacoDiffEditor.tsx # Monaco wrapper
│   │   ├── InlineComments.tsx  # Comment overlay on editor
│   │   ├── CommentThread.tsx   # Single thread UI
│   │   └── CommentForm.tsx     # Add/edit comment form
│   └── ui/
│       ├── Badge.tsx
│       ├── Button.tsx
│       └── Tooltip.tsx
├── hooks/
│   ├── useDiffParser.ts
│   ├── useMonaco.ts
│   └── useComments.ts
├── App.tsx
├── main.tsx
└── index.css
```

**State Management:** Zustand (comments) + local React state (selected file, editor state)

**Data Flow:**
1. Raw unified diff string → `diffParser` → `DiffFile[]`
2. `DiffViewer` selects active `DiffFile` → passes to `MonacoDiffEditor`
3. Monaco renders side-by-side diff with decorations
4. Click on line → opens `CommentForm` anchored to that line
5. Comments stored in Zustand keyed by `fileId:lineNumber`

