### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

## Requirements Analysis

**Core Features:**
- Executive analytics dashboard with KPI metrics cards
- Time-series throughput charts using Recharts
- Optimistic updates via TanStack Query (React Query v5)
- Accessible modal dialogs (WCAG 2.1 AA compliant)
- React 19 with TypeScript strict mode

**Architectural Decisions:**

| Concern | Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| State Management | TanStack Query v5 + React Context | Server state separation from UI state |
| Data Layer | Mock API with realistic latency simulation | Self-contained, no external deps |
| Styling | CSS Modules + CSS custom properties | Zero runtime overhead, themeable |
| Accessibility | ARIA live regions, focus trap, `role=dialog` | WCAG 2.1 AA compliance |
| Type Safety | `strict: true`, discriminated unions, `satisfies` | Zero `any` types |
| Chart | Recharts `ResponsiveContainer` + `ComposedChart` | Responsive, accessible SVG |

**Edge Cases Handled:**
- Empty data states with skeleton loaders
- Network error boundaries with retry logic
- Modal focus trap (Tab/Shift+Tab cycling, Escape key)
- Chart tooltip accessibility (keyboard navigable)
- Optimistic update rollback on server error
- Race conditions in concurrent mutations

**Security Considerations:**
- XSS: All data rendered via React (no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`)
- Input sanitization on filter inputs
- No secrets in client bundle

**File Structure:**
```
src/
├── types/           # Discriminated union types
├── api/             # Mock API layer with latency
├── hooks/           # TanStack Query hooks
├── components/
│   ├── dashboard/   # KPI cards, metric grid
│   ├── charts/      # Throughput chart
│   ├── modal/       # Accessible modal system
│   └── ui/          # Shared primitives
├── contexts/        # Modal + Theme contexts
├── utils/           # Data formatters, validators
└── App.tsx
```

