4. **Inline code review comments** — Click any line to attach a review comment with author, timestamp, and resolution state

### Architecture Decisions

| Concern | Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| State management | Zustand | Lightweight, no boilerplate, perfect for editor state |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS + CSS Modules | Utility-first with scoped component styles |
| Monaco wrapper | `@monaco-editor/react` | Handles loader/worker lifecycle |
| Diff parsing | `diff` npm package | Parses unified diff into structured hunks |
| Type safety | TypeScript strict mode | Catches null/undefined at compile time |
| Comment storage | In-memory Zustand store | No backend required per spec |
| Testing | Vitest + React Testing Library | Fast unit + component tests |

### File Structure
```
src/
  types/           — All shared TypeScript interfaces
  store/           — Zustand state slices
  utils/           — Diff parser, syntax detector, helpers
  components/
    FileTree/      — Left panel: list of changed files
    DiffViewer/    — Monaco-based diff editor pane
    CommentPanel/  — Inline comment threads
    ReviewComment/ — Single comment card
    Toolbar/       — Header with actions
  hooks/           — useComments, useDiffNavigation
  App.tsx
  main.tsx
  index.css
tests/             — Vitest tests
```

### Edge Cases Handled
- Empty diff / no files
- Binary file markers in diff
- Files with only deletions or only additions
- Very long lines (Monaco handles horizontal scroll)
- Comments on context lines vs changed lines
- Comment resolution / re-opening
- File language detection from extension
- Collapsed/expanded file hunks

### Security Considerations
- All comment content is sanitized before render (DOMPurify)
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization
- Monaco editor is sandboxed in iframe-equivalent worker context
- No external network calls — all data is local

