### 1. SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL PLAN

## Requirements Analysis

**Core Features:**
- Real-time terminal output rendering via xterm.js
- Auto-scrolling with user scroll-lock override (stop auto-scroll when user scrolls up)
- Search/filter buffer with highlight matching
- WebSocket connection with exponential backoff reconnection logic
- Full TypeScript strict mode

**Edge Cases:**
- WebSocket message bursts (throttle/buffer writes to xterm)
- Terminal resize (fit addon + window resize observer)
- Search while streaming (live filter against internal ring buffer)
- Reconnection during active search
- Component unmount cleanup (prevent state updates after unmount)
- Binary/malformed WebSocket frames
- Very large buffers (ring buffer with configurable max lines)
- ANSI escape sequence preservation in search results
- Multiple simultaneous search pattern updates (debounce)
- Connection URL validation

**Security Considerations:**
- XSS: xterm.js renders ANSI, not raw HTML — safe by default
- WebSocket URL validation (ws:// or wss:// only)
- No eval, no dangerouslySetInnerHTML
- CSP-compatible output (no inline styles injected dynamically)

**Architecture:**

```
src/
├── types/
│   └── terminal.ts           # All shared TypeScript interfaces/types
├── hooks/
│   ├── useWebSocket.ts        # WebSocket lifecycle + reconnection
│   ├── useTerminal.ts         # xterm.js instance management
│   └── useSearchBuffer.ts     # Ring buffer + search/filter logic
├── components/
│   ├── TerminalViewer.tsx     # Root orchestration component
│   ├── TerminalPane.tsx       # xterm.js DOM mount + resize
│   ├── SearchBar.tsx          # Search input + match navigation
│   └── StatusBar.tsx          # Connection status + stats
├── utils/
│   ├── ansi.ts               # ANSI strip/parse utilities
│   ├── ringBuffer.ts          # Generic ring buffer
│   └── wsReconnect.ts         # Backoff strategy
├── constants.ts
└── index.ts                   # Re-exports
```

**Data Flow:**
```
WebSocket → useWebSocket hook → line buffer → useSearchBuffer
                                                    ↓
                                           filtered lines array
                                                    ↓
                              useTerminal writes filtered output to xterm
                                                    ↓
                                           TerminalPane (DOM)
```

