    │   ├── main.tf
    │   ├── variables.tf
    │   └── outputs.tf
    │
    ├── ecs/                   # Cluster, task definitions, services, IAM roles
    │   ├── main.tf
    │   ├── variables.tf
    │   └── outputs.tf
    │
    ├── elasticache/           # Redis replication group, subnet/param groups
    │   ├── main.tf
    │   ├── variables.tf
    │   └── outputs.tf
    │
    └── cloudwatch/            # Log groups, metric filters, alarms, dashboard
        ├── main.tf
        ├── variables.tf
        └── outputs.tf
```

### Security Design Decisions
- **Principle of Least Privilege**: ECS task role grants only needed actions; execution role grants ECR + SSM + Secrets Manager
- **Network Segmentation**: ALB in public subnets; ECS tasks and ElastiCache in private subnets; no public IPs on tasks
- **Encryption in Transit**: ALB forces HTTPS; ElastiCache has `transit_encryption_enabled = true`; Redis AUTH token via Secrets Manager
- **Encryption at Rest**: ElastiCache `at_rest_encryption_enabled = true`; ECS task ephemeral storage encrypted; CloudWatch logs encrypted via KMS
- **Security Groups**: ALB SG allows 80/443 from internet; ECS SG allows only ALB SG as source; Redis SG allows only ECS SG on port 6379
- **ALB Access Logging**: S3 bucket with server-side encryption, versioning, lifecycle policy
- **Container Insights**: Enabled on ECS cluster for enhanced observability
- **Auto Scaling**: ALB request count and CPU-based ECS service auto scaling

### Edge Cases Handled
- Multi-AZ deployment across 3 AZs for HA
- ALB idle timeout configurable (default 60s)
- HTTP→HTTPS redirect rule at listener level
- Health check grace period for slow-starting containers
- ElastiCache automatic failover with multi-AZ
- CloudWatch alarm actions require SNS topic (created in cloudwatch module)
- Certificate validation with `create_before_destroy` lifecycle
- S3 ALB log bucket policy uses region-specific ELB account IDs
- Task definition revision tracking via `aws_ecs_task_definition` data source

